  {
   "symbol": "d",
   "kind": "note",
   "props": {
    "text": "SUBLEVEL 3 — RESIDENTIAL\n\nQuarters 1 ........ Solace, M. (signals)\nQuarters 2 ........ Voss, E. (Director) + dependant\nQuarters 3 ........ Hale, M. (security)\nCaretaker ......... Ostrowski, B.\n\nDoor codes are set by residents. Forgotten your code? See the caretaker.\nCaretaker's own office code was set by M. Solace, as Mr. Ostrowski 'does not do numbers'.\n\nLaundry: Tues & Fri. PLEASE stop leaving radios on in the laundry.",
    "title": "Residents' directory"
   },
   "sequence": -1,
   "lines": -1
  },
  {
   "symbol": "e",
   "kind": "item",
   "props": {
    "id": "battery"
   },
   "sequence": -1,
   "lines": -1
  },
  {
   "symbol": "f",
   "kind": "note",
   "props": {
    "text": "Tucked into the mirror frame. Dr. Voss, younger than her ID photo, holding a baby up toward the camera. Beside them a young woman, laughing, one hand cupped over the baby's head. Her badge reads SOLACE.\n\nOn the back, in pencil:\n'Danny, 1 yr. Little light. — M.'",
    "title": "Photograph"
   },
   "sequence": 15,
   "lines": -1
  },
  {
   "symbol": "h",
   "kind": "note",
   "props": {
    "text": "Kate —\n\nI'm not allowed to tell you where I am, which is a strange thing to write in a letter I'm not going to send.\n\nThe work here is not what they told me. I won't say more. I'll say this: there's a girl here, Mira, about your age, who carries the Director's boy everywhere like he's her own. Tonight she asked me straight out if I would keep them safe.\n\nI said yes. I'm a man who says yes to that question. You know that about me. I hope you still know it.\n\nIf I don't come home, it's because I kept my word.\n\n— Dad",
    "title": "Unsent letter — M. Hale"
   },
   "sequence": -1,
   "lines": -1
  },
  {
   "symbol": "k",
   "kind": "item",
   "props": {
    "id": "res_key"
   },
   "sequence": 17,
   "lines": -1
  },
  {
   "symbol": "n",
   "kind": "note",
   "props": {
    "text": "SUBLEVEL 3 AMATEUR RADIO CLUB — STATION LOG\n\n02 Feb 98  Antenna re-strung. Lovely clean return off the shelf. Picked up a 1961 shipping forecast.\n14 Mar 98  02:43. Weak voice on 101.3, no call sign:\n           'Is anyone still there? This is Arlen.'\n           Asked for a call sign. Static. (B.O.)\n15 Mar 98  Nobody on site called Arlen. Hale asked me not to write it down again.\n02 Oct 98  Club cabinet code now changes weekly. I read it out on my request show, 92.3, after the one record. Members only — you know who you are.\n\n— B. Ostrowski, Caretaker & Club Secretary",
    "title": "Radio club — station log"
   },
   "sequence": 18,
   "lines": -1
  },
  {
   "symbol": "o",
   "kind": "prop",
   "props": {
    "p": "coat"
   },
   "sequence": -1,
   "lines": -1
  },
  {
   "symbol": "p",
   "kind": "note",
   "props": {
    "text": "A polaroid pinned above the coffee urn. A lopsided cake with one candle. Twelve people in hairnets and lab coats crowded round a high chair, all of them pulling faces at a baby who is pulling one back.\n\nMarker on the white strip:\nHAPPY 1st BIRTHDAY DANNY!!  14.08.98\nlove from the canteen crew",
    "title": "Photo on the canteen wall"
   },
   "sequence": -1,
   "lines": -1
  },
  {
   "symbol": "q",
   "kind": "item",
   "props": {
    "id": "bottle",
